  "key": "pr-1828",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "gh-1826 [BUG] build-mobile wildcard flutter-version 3.47.x re-resolves to uncached patches — daily TestFlight leg dies on the SDK download (fix: exact 3.47.7 pin)",
    "description": "Closes #1826
### Root Cause

`build-mobile.yml`'s `build-ios` (TestFlight) leg passed the wildcard `flutter-version: '3.47.x'` to `setup-flutter-selfhosted`, which resolves the spec against the live releases manifest. Every fresh Flutter patch release re-resolved the wildcard to an SDK not cached on the fa-m5 runner: run 40066130883 (2026-10-24) resolved `3.47.x` → **3.47.8** and the leg died downloading the 2.27 GB SDK inside the bounded curl budget (600s/attempt, 900s total) at 1.48 GB. The desktop lane already pins exact patches (#1431; `build-macos.yml` on 3.47.7 post-#1815) — the mobile lane kept the wildcard, which is why #1735 kept re-opening.

### Fix

- `.github/workflows/build-mobile.yml`: `build-ios` Setup Flutter pin changed `'3.47.x'` → `'3.47.7'` (already in every fa-m5 persistent slot — zero download, subsecond reuse), comment documents the incident and the bump policy; matches the desktop lane.
- `test/setup_flutter_selfhosted_test.dart`: new guard — both self-hosted legs (`build-mobile` `build-ios`, `build-macos` `build-macos`) must pin an exact patch, never a wildcard.

### Test Coverage

- `test/setup_flutter_selfhosted_test.dart` — "self-hosted legs pin an EXACT Flutter patch, never a wildcard (gh-1826)": failed before the fix (`Expected: '3.47.7' / Actual: '3.47.x'`), passes after; file: 28/28 green.
- Sibling workflow-shape guards parsing build-mobile.yml: 304 tests passed.
- Full per-PR suite (`dart test --exclude-tags integration`): **12116 passed, 12 skipped** (macOS `sandbox-exec` live legs not runnable on the Linux host), 0 failures.

### Notes

- No behavioral change for the Android hosted legs (they use subosito on `ubuntu-latest`, untouched).
- Pin bumps must stay conscious/PR-reviewed and match the desktop lane; the guard test enforces exact-patch (no `.x`) on both lanes.
- #1735 auto-closes on the next green daily TestFlight leg (its own mechanism — not closed here)."
  }
